gpio-sim: a released output line keeps driving its last level

Upstream gpio-sim returns every line to its pull when the consumer releases
it. A real SoC GPIO (i.MX8M Plus on Shield) keeps driving an output after
release, so a script that sets a line and exits (`gpioset --toggle 0 ...`)
behaves as on hardware. Inputs still return to their pull.

--- a/gpio-sim-main.c
+++ b/gpio-sim-main.c
@@ -221,8 +221,9 @@
 	struct gpio_sim_chip *chip = gpiochip_get_data(gc);
 
 	scoped_guard(mutex, &chip->lock) {
-		__assign_bit(offset, chip->value_map,
-			     !!test_bit(offset, chip->pull_map));
+		if (test_bit(offset, chip->direction_map))
+			__assign_bit(offset, chip->value_map,
+				     !!test_bit(offset, chip->pull_map));
 		__clear_bit(offset, chip->request_map);
 	}
 }
